commit 2da2189c5b40c298aa0b9d7bf545e001b081ee60
Author: wave7-agent <agent@rickylabs.dev>
Date:   Fri Sep 4 12:36:14 2026 +0200

    Design: act on the vision critique — widget vocabulary, money correctness, soft elevation
    
    Ranked items 1-6 of design-steer-2, in the order the critic ranked them.
    
    Buttons (1): every `3px 3px 0` offset shadow and its `translate(1px,1px)`
    nudge is gone, along with the same fingerprint in toast.css and
    desktop-update-prompt.css. Elevation is diffuse and token-driven; a new
    `pill` variant gives the reference cards' hairline capsule action.
    
    New components (2, 3, 5, 6), each with its own stylesheet:
      · DeltaChip      — tinted pill + directional glyph, rendered on the hero
                         number's own baseline instead of in the card header.
      · SemicircularGauge — 180° two-tone arc, `stroke-linecap="butt"` so the
                         terminals are flat cuts flush with the baseline and the
                         segment junction is a crisp radial cut.
      · SegmentedControl  — the selected cell is a filled pill (C4), never a
                         border change; buttons for local state, links for a range
                         that lives in the URL.
      · ComparisonAreaChart — hand-authored SVG, comparison period as a
                         translucent layer under a stroked current series (H5),
                         CSS-only crosshair + dark pointer bubble (H4).
      · FooterColumns  — N equal columns divided by hairline rules (C5).
      · WidgetCard     — the 5-band compound card; the header row is restored
                         through the `class` seam, not a fork (T4).
      · MoneyText      — the one renderer for an amount. Formats nothing itself:
                         every digit comes from moneyParts(). `100` renders
                         $100.00 and the currency is a prefix in its own element,
                         never concatenated as `100.00USD`.
    
    Tokens (T1: json is the source, css generated, both edited together):
    radius-3xl 24px for the containing card, shadow-ambient for its diffuse
    elevation, tip-bg/tip-fg so a chart readout inverts against the card in both
    themes, destructive-hover and control-thumb so no component touches a ramp
    step. That last point is the fix for the dark-mode defect: the paper ramp
    inverts, so `--ns-paper-12` is near-black in light and near-white in dark.
    
    Gallery: the seven new items have their own `ledgerlineCatalog` rather than
    being folded into `registryMeta.total`, which stays a fact about fresh-ui.
    Every scaffold string in the gallery (api-gateway, eu-west, v2.4.1) is
    replaced with a real Ledgerline value. RangeControlDemo is an island that
    owns only the selected range and re-projects data already on the page (D5).
    
    DESIGN.md gains the rules this work had to decide: M8/M9 (one money
    renderer; a hero is not coloured by direction), C7/C8 (radius encodes
    containment; no offset shadow), H6/H8/H9 (one hairline frame; flat arc
    caps; the comparison layer shares the current hue), T2a (no component
    touches a ramp step), R3 (app-owned catalog is separate).
    
    tests/design_contract_test.ts makes the checkable ones run: it caught two
    offset shadows and three ramp-step leaks the critic did not open the files
    for, and it holds tokens.json and tokens.css to the same variable set.

