[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing && git add apps/ledgerline-web/components/product/money-text.tsx apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/money-text.css && git -c core.pager=cat commit -q -F - <<'EOF' 2>&1 | tail -3
Fix: the product's money renderer printed $100 and 100.00USD

Every amount in Ledgerline went through this component — invoices, ledger
balances, run items — and it formatted them itself:

  const parsed = Number(text);                       // float round-trip
  const decimals = text.includes('.') ? ... : 0;
  minimumFractionDigits: Math.min(decimals, 6)       // "100" -> 0 decimals

so an integer hundred rendered as `$100` where the ledger requires
`$100.00`, and the currency was appended straight onto the digits as
`100.00USD`. It also re-derived direction with `amount > 0`, which is a fact
the money layer already resolves.

MoneyText now formats nothing. It makes one `moneyParts()` call and renders
the parts it is handed, so there is exactly one place where a decimal becomes
text. Verified by rendering:

  '100' + USD   -> <span class="ns-money-text__currency">$</span>100.00
  '-1204.5'     -> $-1,204.50     data-money-sign="neg"
  '0.005'       -> $0.005         metered precision survives
  null          -> —              plus sr-only "not measured"

The currency is a prefix element spaced by layout, never a concatenated code.
The stylesheet follows it: the suffix margin becomes a 1px gap, and an amount
is nowrap so a column of figures keeps its decimal alignment.

`data-money-sign` and `data-money='absent'` are preserved — routes and the
stylesheet select on them.

Refs design-steer-2 item 4.
EOF
