Fix: the exception chip went unreadable in dark mode

The chip reached past the semantic layer into a ramp step:

  color: var(--ns-rust-6);      /* oklch(54.5%) — ~3.4:1 on a dark card */
  background: color-mix(... var(--ns-rust-6) 10% ...);
  border: 1px solid color-mix(... var(--ns-rust-6) 24% ...);

The paper ramp inverts between themes, so a ramp step is never a component's
colour. On a dark card (`--ns-paper-10`, 21.5% L) rust-6 lands near 3.4:1,
under the 4.5:1 a chip's text needs.

All three now come from semantic tokens the theme re-steps itself:
`--ns-money-neg` (rust-6 in light, rust-4 at 70.5% in dark, ~5.7:1) and the
`--ns-destructive-subtle` / `--ns-destructive-border` pair, which steps 10/20%
up to 12/24% in dark. One rule covers both themes, so there is no
dark-mode override to drift out of sync.

Refs design-steer-2 "also flagged".

Note on the critique: it reported rust-6 as 45.5% lightness. It is 54.5% —
45.5% is rust-7. The finding stands, the number was one step off.
EOF
