[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing && git add apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/button.css apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/toast.css apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/desktop-update-prompt.css apps/ledgerline-web/assets/ui/sheet.css apps/ledgerline-web/components/ui/button.tsx && git -c core.pager=cat commit -q -F - <<'EOF' 2>&1 | tail -3
Fix: drop the brutalist offset shadows, add the pill action

Every action carried a hard-edged offset shadow that shrank on press:

  box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--ns-primary) 55%, var(--ns-paper-12));
  transform: translate(1px, 1px);   /* hover */
  transform: translate(2px, 2px);   /* active */

That is a retro-brutalist treatment the reference cards do not use — they
carry soft, hairline-bordered capsules — and in dark mode it inverted into a
defect: the offsets are mixed from `--ns-paper-12`, which is 13.5% lightness
in light and near-white in dark, so every action grew a stark pale slab on a
dark surface. The same fingerprint was in toast.css (4px, mixed from
`--ns-border-strong`) and desktop-update-prompt.css (2px).

All of it is gone. Press now reads as a dip in brightness, which works on both
grounds, and hover moves the border on the variants that have one.

`pill` is added as a variant so the capsule the references actually use is
available rather than hand-rolled at each call site: full radius, hairline
border, tinted hover, no offset.

Two things this commit deliberately does not do:

  · switch.css still paints its thumb with `--ns-paper-12`. A thumb that stays
    light in both themes cannot be expressed with a ramp step, and the token
    that names it (`--ns-control-thumb`) is not here. It needs a token-layer
    decision, not a substitution.
  · sheet.css keeps an omnidirectional shadow. The design branch has a proper
    directional `--ns-shadow-drawer`; this tree does not, so the panel uses
    `--ns-shadow-xl` and the paper-12 leak is gone.

Refs design-steer-2 ranked item 1.
EOF
